<title>USA: BPA raises Wed peak firm prices by 50 cents a MWh.</title>
<headline>BPA raises Wed peak firm prices by 50 cents a MWh.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) continued to offer only peak firm power for Wednesday pre-schedulings, while raising prices by 50 cents per megawatt hour (MWh), the agency said Tuesday.</p>
<p>BPA offered 200 MW of peak firm power at $18.50 per MWh for Northwest deliveries and $20.50 for California-Oregon border (COB) sales.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau, +1 213 955 6761))</p>
